    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363">

                <pb facs="0365" n="357" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg357"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.51/1477a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-06-08T15:00:00-04:00">June 8, 1939—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>106. Do you have any further indication as to intention of Brazilian Government
                    in regard to resumption payment on dollar bonds on July 1?<anchor n="18"
                        xml:id="d363-f1"/> Time for possible discussion is getting very short.
                    Failure to afford opportunity for such discussion will be regrettable.</p>
                <p>Please report by cable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d363-f1" n="18" xml:id="d363-f1-content">
                <p>See paragraph numbered V in letter from the Brazilian Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs, March 8, <ref target="#pg352">p. 352</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
